      "writtenOn": "2021-01-13T06:08:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to get a little more crisp. about how this will work.\n\nIf the caller specifies count \u003e 1, but KM can only enforce count \u003d\u003d 1,\n\n(a) Is the tag in the returned KeyCharacteristics? If so, with what value?\n(b) Is the tag in the attestation certificate (if requested)?  If so, in which authorization list and with what value?\n\nIf the caller specifies count \u003e\u003d 1, but KM can\u0027t enforce it at all, same questions.\n\nNote the almost-landed changes in KeyCharacteristics in aosp/1544908\n\nA related question:  How does the app developer know whether KM cannot enforce this, can enforce count \u003d\u003d 1 or count \u003e 1?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 346,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "a5367fea30a718aaaf1460c83da20d5e8add35da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60b1cc7f_a483bfb0",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/Tag.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 14
